Arithmetic sequences of integers with first term 4 containing 24 and 34: common difference d must divide 20 and 30, so d divides gcd(20,30)=10, and d>0 (since 24>4). Also d could be negative? If d<0, terms decrease from 4, never reaching 24. d=0 gives constant 4. So d ∈ {1,2,5,10}.

10th term = 4 + 9d. Sum = 4·4 + 9(1+2+5+10) = 16 + 162 = 178.

\boxed{178}

